{"id":"u-58d21f1f-9f2c-47bc-aaf0-53dfb2cbf815","src":"community","title":"The King Program","author":"Dean Daoud","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/c6N2Sn-the-king-program","desc":"Have you ever thought ‘what is the least amount of effort I can put into gym and still get gains’? This is that program. Is basically 5x5. But 3 sets on any exercise that can be deemed hard. Any hard exercise like squat, bent over row or deadlift is swapped out for a much easier alternative and you can start on the lowest weight you want. \n\nStart bench on 20kg (just the bar); machine row on the lowest weight possible; leg press on the lowest weight possible; overhead press on 20kg (just the bar); leg curl on the lowest weight possible.\nStart on these low weights and each session increase the weight by 1-2.5kg. So let’s say bench press, the first session is 20kg, then the next session is 25kg (or even 22kg if you want to increase it slower) then, 30, 35 and so on (or 24, 26 and so on).\nWith the machine exercises, you just increase the weight by the minimum weight. \n\nIt’s super easy. The first 1-2 months will be such minimal effort and the program will transition from super easy, to challenging, slowly over the weeks, so you won’t even feel the effort change. Or if you do, it’s so slow that you can prepare yourself for it. \n\nIn terms of diet. Just focus on eating either 1gram of protein per pound of body weight or 1gram of protein per cm of height. \nSo if you’re 180 pounds in weight and 173 cm. You can either eat 180grams of protein or 173grams. \nUsually if you’re on the fatter side you eat your height in protein and if you’re on the skinner you eat your weight in protein.","level":["Beginner"],"goals":["Muscle"],"equipment":["Garage Gym"],"minutes":50,"joins":1,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-06-04T18:02:53.886Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Workout A","Workout B","Workout A"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Leg Press","sets":[{"r":5,"x":5}]},{"n":"Bench Press (Bar